    "created_at": "2024-07-10T20:13:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-10T20:13:30Z",
    "body": "The explainer now includes [Permissions API integration](https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/html-fullscreen-without-a-gesture?tab=readme-ov-file#permissions-api-integration).\r\n\r\nUsing that [Permissions API](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/) signal and HTML's definition of [transient activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#transient-activation) (which is web-exposed via [The UserActivation interface](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#the-useractivation-interface)), seems beneficial for spec clarity, debuggability, and feature detection. Implying transient activation in this specific case from a browser setting seems lacking in those traits.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fullscreen/issues/comments/2221352544/reactions",
